/target
# Any nested target/ as well: tests/consumer/ is its own package, and its build
# products (419 files, 76 MiB) were once committed because only the root was
# anchored. Keep the anchored form too — it documents the intent.
target/
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock
.idea/
# trybuild scratch (recreated on snapshot mismatch)
/wip/
# local Rust 2024 feature notes (project-adjacent reference, not packaged)
/rust-2024-feature.md
# Python bytecode: the model suite is Python, and its `__pycache__/` was committed once -
# four `.pyc` files that change on every run and on every interpreter bump, so running the
# suite dirtied the tree. Ignored here and removed from the index; the files stay on disk.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
